<title>USA: Shell says U.S. Capline December nominations rise.</title>
<headline>Shell says U.S. Capline December nominations rise.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil said Monday that December crude oil nominations on the Capline pipeline, which acts as a key oil artery running through the U.S. Midwest, increased from the previous month.</p>
<p>Nominations for December were 962,792 barrels per day (bpd), around 20,000 bpd more than actual November volumes at 942,608 bpd, Shell said.</p>
<p>November nominations, not the actual volumes, were slated at 965,612 bpd, down around 3,100 bpd from actual October volumes and well off the October nominations of 1,001,209 bpd.</p>
<p>Capline has a total capacity of about 1.1 to 1.2 million bpd, and Shell Oil, a unit of the Royal Dutch/Shell Group is operator of the line.</p>
<p>-Patrick Connole, New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828</p>
